Subject: Improve-Async-Scheduler-Throughput

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Vanilla async scheduler tasks are executed on a fixed thread pool
that shares threads with other server components. This limits
throughput when many plugins schedule long-running async tasks and
can cause cascading delays when threads are blocked.

Impact:
Higher async task throughput. Better isolation between async tasks
from different plugins. No thread starvation from long-running
async operations.

Migration Note:
This patch enables VeltisMC's virtual-thread-based async scheduler.
Each plugin gets its own dedicated virtual thread for task execution.
Virtual threads are lightweight and scale to thousands of concurrent
tasks without thread pool exhaustion.

